                    1118.0,
                    682.0
                ],
                [
                    315.0,
                    682.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 In AC power grids the frequency is the result of the collective behavior of all connected devices. The frequency is always drifting unless perfect equilibrium has been reached. The grid is typically never running at exactly the EVSENominalFrequency. The EVSENominalFrequency only defines a theoretical target frequency and provides a reference point for the definition of technical requirements which define the detection of and the reaction to abnormal situations. However, in some situations (power grid emergencies, small power islands, etc.) the desired frequency for the equilibrium point intentionally gets pushed outside the normal operating bandwidth. Only in those situations the EVSETargetFrequency can be used. The goal of the EVSETargetFrequency is to communicate the equilibrium point and to enable the EV's power inverter to operate in a robust way under extreme circumstances.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                707,
                1123,
                897
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
